1
00:01:16,666 --> 00:01:22,666
Pixie Hollow Games is a animation, family film directed by Bradley Raymond.

2
00:02:33,333 --> 00:02:39,333
Rosetta and new arrival Chloe band together to try to break the garden fairies' legendary losing streak in the Pixie
Hollow Games, a sports spectacle filled with pixie pageantry, fantastic fairy events and hilarious surprises.

3
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:56,000
Rosetta (voice), played by Megan Hilty.

4
00:05:06,666 --> 00:05:12,666
Glimmer (voice), played by Tiffany Thornton.

5
00:06:23,333 --> 00:06:29,333
Fern (voice), played by Zendaya.

6
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:46,000
Rumble (voice), played by Jason Dolley.

7
00:08:56,666 --> 00:09:02,666
Chloe (voice), played by Brenda Song.

8
00:10:13,333 --> 00:10:19,333
Tinker Bell (voice), played by Mae Whitman.

9
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:36,000
Pixie Hollow Games is a 23-minute animated television special
broadcast on November 19, 2011, on Disney Channel.

10
00:12:46,666 --> 00:12:52,666
Based on the Disney Fairies franchise, it was produced by
Disneytoon Studios and animated by Prana Studios.

11
00:14:03,333 --> 00:14:09,333
It features the voices of Mae Whitman, Lucy Liu, Raven-Symoné, Megan Hilty, Angela Bartys, and others, as Tinker
Bell and the other fairies of Pixie Hollow in Never Land, taking part in an Olympic-style competition.

12
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:26,000
It is based loosely on J.

13
00:16:36,666 --> 00:16:42,666
Barrie's Peter Pan stories, by way of Disney's animated adaptation.

14
00:17:53,333 --> 00:17:59,333
It was originally intended as the last of five feature-length films in the Tinker Bell series of direct-to-DVD 3D
animated films, with the title Tinker Bell: Race through the Seasons, and a release date in 2012.

15
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:16,000
However, the movie was rescheduled and retooled as a TV
special instead of a film-length movie.

16
00:20:26,666 --> 00:20:32,666
Unlike the previous feature films in this series, Tinker Bell is not a central
featured character in this special release, which is focused on Rosetta.

17
00:21:43,333 --> 00:21:49,333
The film explores themes of sports, magic,
competition, fairy tale, olympic games.
